# Names only. Never real values. Copy to .env for local development.
#
# `.env` is git-ignored. `npm start` and `npm run dev` read it if it is there
# (node --env-file-if-exists), so this is where a rotated credential goes.

# The practice credential for the rotation exercise: a classic GitHub personal
# access token on your OWN account, with NO scopes ticked.
#
# Leave this blank to begin with. Blank is a normal state — the app starts and
# prints `practice credential: not set`.
#
# When you rotate, the NEW token goes here, in this git-ignored file, and NOT
# back into src/lib/github.js where the old one came from. A value here wins
# over the one in that file, which is the point: that is what "deploy the
# replacement" means on this app.
GITHUB_TOKEN=
